<section class="shell faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="faq-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
    <h2 id="faq-title">A few useful definitions.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-list">
    <article class="faq-item">
      <h3>Why cohort-based?</h3>
      <p>
        So the commitment is real but finite. The first cohort runs across four monthly themes,
        then we refresh. That keeps the group small, intentional, and easier to say yes to.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="faq-item">
      <h3>What is a build club?</h3>
      <p>
        Every month, the group builds around one theme, tool, problem, or question. You explore it
        in your own time, then come back to show what you made, what broke, and what you learned.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="faq-item">
      <h3>What is a Marketing Engineer?</h3>
      <p>
        A marketing engineer is a marketer who got tired of waiting for someone else to build the
        thing they need. It is an emerging role that combines taste and curiosity with technical
        ability: writing scripts, connecting APIs, spinning up agents, and transforming manual
        processes into systems that scale.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="faq-item">
      <h3>What about people outside New York?</h3>
      <p>
        Our end goal is to build a global community for marketing engineers who want to swap ideas,
        notes, and demos, both in person and online. Our first cohort will be focused in NYC so we
        can test out the format and iterate before scaling.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
